silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_04_yoneda_for_transport_sections_03_profile_collapse_pathology_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'ProfileCollapsePathologyConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the clinic 'patient visit' arrow that aggregates both household interactions without date discrimination; also, a derived anchor for the transport diagram: the clinic-side image of the household typed leg, carrying composition data.." .
